<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.1 · Slayer Foundation & While Guthix Sleeps" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-1" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.1</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Slayer Foundation &amp; While Guthix Sleeps</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Explore Mos Le'Harmless, complete The Path of Glouphrie, and prepare for While Guthix Sleeps. Use the quest rewards along the way to shorten your Slayer, Magic and Thieving training.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Rum Deal → Cabin Fever → Great Brain Robbery → 56 Slayer, 60 Strength and 56 Thieving → Path of Glouphrie → 58 Slayer, 67 Magic and 72 Thieving → While Guthix Sleeps."
        stats={["Use each quest's lamps before starting the next training session", "Unboosted 60 Strength, 58 Slayer, 67 Magic and 72 Thieving before WGS", "A black mask and other rare drops are optional upgrades"]}
        unlocks={["Holy wrench and Mos Le'Harmless/Cave Horror access", "Poison Waste Dungeon and its spirit-tree destination", "Ancient Guthixian Temple and normal Tormented Demons after WGS"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Your goals for Chapter 3:</strong> finish every currently released quest, earn a Fire Cape, and build the transport, supplies and boss experience to choose your next adventure. Bowfa/crystal, raids, gear hunts, diaries, Combat Achievements, collection log, relaxed progression and eventual 99s are optional Endgame Paths. You can finish this guide without waiting for rare drops, including an Enhanced Crystal Weapon Seed.</div>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Before starting:</strong> check your skills and equipment from Chapter 2. You should have at least <strong>51 Slayer, 66 Magic and 60 Attack</strong>, Attack + Strength ≥130, 70 Prayer and Defence, Piety, a dragon defender, Barrows gloves, Helm of Neitiznot, Proselyte, an upgraded Iban's staff and 70+ Herblore. Recover any missing equipment or finish its earlier step before continuing. Keep your full Rogue outfit from Chapter 1 for the Thieving sessions below; your Thieving level will depend on how much cash you earned there. <strong>Check Strength separately:</strong> The Path of Glouphrie needs an unboosted 60 even if your Attack + Strength total already reaches 130. Use your own Hitpoints and combat level when choosing fights and Slayer masters. The steps below cover the remaining Slayer, Magic and Thieving training for While Guthix Sleeps.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Pirate chain · useful rewards first</div><h2>Complete three quests before returning to Slayer.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i31-rum-deal" number="1" title="Complete Rum Deal; keep the Holy wrench">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> Rum Deal starts the pirate chain for Cabin Fever, pays <strong>7,000 XP each in Prayer, Farming and Fishing</strong>, and awards the Holy wrench. Earlier steps covered Zogre Flesh Eaters, Priest in Peril and the unboosted levels needed: 42 Slayer, 42 Crafting, 40 Farming, 47 Prayer and 50 Fishing. Begin with <strong>Pirate Pete at the dock north-east of the Ectofuntus</strong>; the Ectophial makes the approach easy. Bring ordinary combat gear, food, a teleport and a way to attack from a distance for the level-150 Evil spirit and diseased fever spider. Pack a <strong>rake, seed dibber and Slayer gloves</strong>; obtain the quest bucket on Braindeath Island. Have at least 47 current Prayer points when Davey blesses the wrench. Protect from Melee or safespot the Evil spirit; wear the Slayer gloves when fighting the fever spider to prevent its disease. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Rum_Deal" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest details</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Tools and disease protection before Pirate Pete" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Buy missing <strong>Slayer gloves from a Slayer equipment shop</strong> and keep them equipped for the fever spider. Withdraw the rake and seed dibber from a tool leprechaun; if never bought, <strong>Sarah at the farm south of Falador</strong> sells both. Check your bank and leprechaun storage before buying replacements.</p>
          <p>Restore Prayer at an altar before sailing: Davey needs you to have <strong>47 Prayer points remaining</strong> when he blesses the wrench. If combat potions are missing, use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>potion recipes and ingredient sources</a>; an ordinary restore potion treats drained stats and <strong>does not restore Prayer</strong>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Retain the Holy wrench.</strong> In your inventory it improves Prayer-potion restoration; bank it when the inventory slot matters more. There is no requirement to carry it constantly.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i31-cabin-fever" number="2" title="Complete Cabin Fever; open Mos Le'Harmless">
        <p>Continue to <strong>Bill Teach at The Green Ghost inn in Port Phasmatys</strong>. Pirate's Treasure, Rum Deal, Big Chompy Bird Hunting, Zogre Flesh Eaters, Jungle Potion, Druidic Ritual and Priest in Peril are already complete; you also have the unboosted 42 Agility, 45 Crafting, 50 Smithing and 40 Ranged needed. Bring food and ordinary combat gear for level-57 pirates, and leave roughly <strong>11 free inventory spaces</strong> for the supplies found aboard the ships. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Cabin_Fever" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Use the ship's supplies" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>The repair and boarding materials come from <strong>Bill Teach's ship and the enemy ship during the quest</strong>: take the rope, repair planks, tacks, paste and cannon supplies from the relevant stores when asked. There is no need to buy a separate construction batch for this quest. Keep the <strong>11 free spaces</strong> for those items, and bank before boarding if food and equipment fill the inventory.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>The payoff is <strong>Mos Le'Harmless and access to its Cave Horror cave</strong>, which makes the later black-mask option possible. The charter-ship discount and Trouble Brewing access are bonuses, not new errands. You can return by speaking to Bill Teach at Port Phasmatys; the Ectophial is a convenient return leg.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i31-brain-robbery" number="3" title="Complete The Great Brain Robbery; put its 5,000-XP lamp into Slayer">
        <p>Start with <strong>Brother Tranquility on Mos Le'Harmless</strong>. Creature of Fenkenstrain, Cabin Fever and Recipe for Disaster's Pirate Pete subquest are complete; you also meet the unboosted 50 Prayer and Crafting/Construction requirements. Gather the supplies below and withdraw them for each phase: <strong>fishbowl helmet plus diving apparatus</strong> (or a medallion of the deep), <strong>ring of charos</strong>, holy symbol, an <strong>ordinary hammer and 200 nails</strong> (100 for the stairs and 100 for the crate), and <strong>18 normal planks</strong> if you must make the ten wooden cats yourself. The cats also take <strong>ten ordinary furs</strong> at <strong>Crafting table 1 or better</strong> in a POH Workshop's clockmaking space. If the table is absent, add <strong>four oak planks and a saw</strong> to build it; allow <strong>10,000 coins</strong> for the Workshop room itself if that is also missing. Buy missing ordinary furs from <strong>Pellem's Fur Store in the south-east Hunter Guild</strong> (three stocked, replenishing over time), and take 18 normal logs to a sawmill and pay 100 coins per normal plank. The 18 normal planks cover ten cats plus the quest's eight other planks; do not carry them all through every trip. Reclaim missing diving gear from Murphy at Port Khazard or the ring from Fenkenstrain as the quest allows. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Great_Brain_Robbery/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current item and phase checklist</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Make only the missing cats, planks and holy symbol" label="Quest preparation">
          <p><strong>Check how many wooden cats you already have.</strong> Each missing cat takes <strong>one normal plank and one fur</strong> at <strong>Crafting table 1 or better</strong> (16 Crafting). Keep <strong>eight further normal planks</strong> for the quest itself. If making all ten cats, that is 18 planks and ten furs; the table's <strong>four oak planks</strong> are a separate, one-time setup cost at 16 Construction. A missing Workshop room costs <strong>10,000 coins</strong> and requires 15 Construction, which you reached earlier. A sawmill converts four oak logs for 250 coins each. Buy the <strong>200 nails</strong> and any missing saw from the sawmill operator. Bring an ordinary hammer: Fenkenstrain keeps it and will not accept an Imcando hammer.</p>
          <p>If the <strong>holy symbol</strong> is missing, use a holy-symbol mould and <strong>one silver bar</strong> at a furnace, add <strong>one ball of wool</strong> to the unstrung symbol, then ask <strong>Brother Jered upstairs in Edgeville Monastery</strong> to bless it. Dommik in Al Kharid sells the mould; mine one silver ore at the south-west Varrock mine and smelt it, then shear and spin one sheep's wool at Lumbridge if those inputs are missing. Your Crafting and Smithing levels are sufficient, and you have the 31 Prayer needed to speak to Jered.</p>
          <p>Bank any follower <strong>and any pet in the inventory</strong> before diving. Recover the fishbowl helmet and diving apparatus from <strong>Murphy at Port Khazard</strong> if they were discarded. Prepare the fight's Prayer potions through the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>local potion recovery route</a>; make only the current trip's missing supplies and restock between attempts.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Barrelchest warning:</strong> the level-190 fight can drain and switch off Prayer, so do not assume uninterrupted Protect from Melee. Bring several Prayer potions, roughly ten good food and a ranged/Magic setup if you want the current entrance/corner safespot; do <em>not</em> hide directly behind a pew, where the anchor's ground strike can still hit. It is not undead, so Salve is no help. If you die, reclaiming items may require another underwater set; plan that before a second attempt. The anchor is a reward, <strong>not a mandatory weapon upgrade</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Great_Brain_Robbery" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Fight and reward reference</a>.</p>
        <p>Claim the direct <strong>6,000 Prayer, 3,000 Crafting and 2,000 Construction XP</strong>. Use the selectable <strong>5,000-XP blessed lamp on Slayer immediately</strong> to shorten the training for The Path of Glouphrie. Check your Slayer XP afterward; your Herblore is already high enough for the coming quests.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Slayer · prepare for Path of Glouphrie</div><h2>Train to 56 Slayer and 60 Strength.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i31-slayer-56" number="4" title="Reach 56 Slayer and check that Strength is at least 60">
        <p>After using the Brain Robbery lamp, check your <strong>Slayer XP</strong> and complete tasks until you reach <strong>56 Slayer</strong>. If you are below <strong>60 Strength</strong>, use your dragon scimitar's aggressive/Strength style during those tasks. If Slayer reaches 56 first, finish the remaining Strength training afterward. The Path of Glouphrie requires both levels without boosts.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i31-slayer-methods" skill="Slayer" target="56 Slayer + 60 Strength, unboosted" why="The Path of Glouphrie needs both levels and awards more Slayer and Strength XP afterward." recommended="Nieve, if your combat level is at least 85: take normal assignments and train combat alongside Slayer." relaxed="Another appropriate Slayer master is fine if you prefer their tasks; finish ordinary assignments at your own pace." informational={true} />
        <p><strong>Your first tasks:</strong> Nieve stands by the Stronghold Slayer Cave and southern bank in the <strong>Tree Gnome Stronghold</strong>; use the spirit tree to the Stronghold and run south-west. She requires <strong>85 combat</strong>; if you are below that, use an eligible master such as Chaeldar. Ask for a task, bring its required Slayer equipment, kill the assigned monsters and return for the next task. Ordinary assignments with your existing gear are enough here; a cannon, barrage spells, task bracelets, block list or point-boosting routine is optional. <strong>Stop at 56 Slayer;</strong> complete Path before training toward 58 so its reward reduces the work left. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Nieve" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Nieve access</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i31-path" number="5" title="Complete The Path of Glouphrie and claim all four fixed XP lamps">
        <p><strong>Before starting:</strong> check that you have unboosted <strong>56 Slayer, 60 Strength, 56 Thieving, 47 Ranged and 45 Agility</strong>, plus The Eyes of Glouphrie, Waterfall Quest and Tree Gnome Village. Earlier chapters covered Ranged, Agility and those quests, and the previous step covered Slayer and Strength. If your <strong>Thieving is below 56</strong>, train with Wealthy Citizens/Stealing Valuables or Ardougne Knights, wearing your full Rogue outfit, and stop at 56. Begin with <strong>King Bolren in Tree Gnome Village</strong>. Use the spirit tree/gnome network for early stages, then <strong>fairy ring BKP</strong> and run north-west toward Longramble in the Galarpos Mountains. Bring food, combat gear, a crossbow and mith grapple for the crossing; keep the quest's crystal chime for the warped enemies in the Poison Waste Dungeon. Quest Helper can handle the coloured-shape puzzles. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Path_of_Glouphrie" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest and requirement reference</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Where to buy a crossbow and find the dungeon key if needed" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>If the ranged slot is empty, <strong>Nardok in the Dorgeshuun mine</strong> sells the Dorgeshuun crossbow after The Lost Tribe; it works for the grapple crossing. A rune crossbow is unnecessary. Buy a feather from a fishing shop if making the bolt, and use the mithril-bar recipe below only for the missing grapple.</p>
          <p>You can skip Quest Helper's Tree Gnome Village dungeon key after completing <strong>Roving Elves and Song of the Elves</strong>, as you did earlier in this guide. If the quest still asks you for it, search the <strong>north-east crate in the Tree Gnome Village dungeon</strong>. Keep the quest-made crystal chime until the warped-creature fights are finished.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>If no mith grapple is banked:</strong> at an anvil, use a hammer and <strong>one mithril bar</strong> to smith a mith grapple tip (59 Smithing; no mould). If no finished mithril bolt is banked, smith <strong>a second mithril bar into unfinished mithril bolts</strong> and feather one. Attach the tip to that <strong>one mithril bolt</strong> at 59 Fletching, then add <strong>one rope</strong> bought from Ned in Draynor Village. You reached both skill levels in Chapter 2. Check for the finished grapple before leaving, then equip it as ammunition and a crossbow in the weapon slot for the crossing. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mith_grapple" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Grapple recipe</a>.</p>
        <p>At the dungeon, use the crystal chime as directed against warped terrorbirds; take food and Protect from Missiles, and use the rooms/doorways to isolate the final group if needed. Finish the quest and <strong>use all four fixed lamps now:</strong> <strong>20,000 Slayer, 30,000 Strength, 5,000 Magic and 5,000 Thieving XP</strong>. These rewards are lamps to claim, not automatic XP to assume. Path completes a major WGS prerequisite and opens the <strong>Poison Waste Dungeon and a spirit-tree destination</strong>; warped-creature tasks can be unlocked later. Neither a warped sceptre nor any other drop is required. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Path_of_Glouphrie#Rewards" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Verified rewards</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i31-slayer-58" number="6" title="Resume Slayer tasks and stop at 58">
        <p>Check your Slayer XP <strong>after using Path's 20,000-XP lamp</strong>. If you started Path at exactly level 56 (<strong>184,040 XP</strong>), you now have at least <strong>204,040 XP</strong>; level 57 begins at 203,254 and level 58 at 224,466. You therefore need at most <strong>20,426 more Slayer XP</strong>, and less if you started with more XP. Resume ordinary tasks and <strong>stop at 58 Slayer</strong>. This opens Cave Horrors and brings you closer to the eventual Quest Cape requirement of 74; the rest of that training comes later.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i31-black-mask" title="Black mask — recommended, optional and resumable" optional={true}>
        <p>At 58 Slayer with Cabin Fever complete, you <em>may</em> try for a black mask from <strong>Cave Horrors</strong> (about <strong>1/512</strong> per kill). The mask's on-task melee accuracy/damage bonus and later Slayer-helmet use make it valuable during the eventual 58→74 journey, but <strong>the Quest Cape / Fire Cape route does not wait here for the drop</strong>. Try a short session if you want the upgrade. If it drops, great; otherwise leave and return in a future Slayer mood. No kill count, helmet unlock or Slayer-point purchase is mandatory. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Killing_cave_horror" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cave Horror reference</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>First trip:</strong> take Bill Teach's boat from Port Phasmatys to Mos Le'Harmless, then run east to the Mos Le'Harmless Cave. Bring a <strong>lit light source and witchwood icon</strong> (buy the icon from a Slayer master if absent); keep the icon equipped until you have other valid scream protection. Use ordinary melee gear, food and Prayer as needed; Cave Horrors' attacks can hurt through unsuitable melee armour, so a modest Ranged/dragonhide setup or the entrance safespot is also fine. Bank useful herbs/seeds, nature runes and alchable equipment; leave junk. Stop whenever the session ceases to be fun.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Magic · prepare for While Guthix Sleeps</div><h2>Use Path's Magic lamp, then train to 67.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i31-magic-67" number="7" title="Reach 67 Magic for While Guthix Sleeps">
        <p>Check your Magic XP <strong>after using Path's 5,000-XP lamp</strong>. If you finished Chapter 2 with <strong>514,111 XP</strong>, the lamp brings you to <strong>519,111 XP</strong>; level 67 begins at <strong>547,953 XP</strong>, leaving <strong>28,842 XP</strong>. Your own training and spell use may have brought you closer, or already to 67. If using High Level Alchemy, divide your remaining XP by 65 and round up to find the casts needed—about <strong>444 casts</strong> in that example. High Alchemy requires the <strong>standard spellbook</strong>. Use profitable or break-even items and nature runes you already have, then choose another method if those supplies run out.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i31-magic-methods" skill="Magic" target="67, unboosted" why="While Guthix Sleeps requires 67 Magic. The quests needing 75 come later." recommended="Use High Alchemy on profitable or break-even items you already have, with nature runes and the standard spellbook." relaxed="Cast ordinary combat Magic on a low-risk target or a suitable Slayer task; the upgraded Iban's staff remains available." informational={true} />
        <p><strong>Stop at 67 Magic.</strong> You can leave Mage Training Arena rewards for another time; train to 75 when preparing for Dragon Slayer II and Desert Treasure II later.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Grandmaster finale</div><h2>Bank by phase; then solve the fights deliberately.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i31-wgs" number="8" title="Complete While Guthix Sleeps and claim its permanent rewards">
        <p><strong>First, reach 72 Thieving:</strong> use Path's <strong>5,000 Thieving-XP lamp</strong>, then check your level. If you are below 72, train with relaxed Wealthy Citizens/Stealing Valuables or familiar Ardougne Knights, wearing your full Rogue outfit from Chapter 1. <strong>Stop at an unboosted 72.</strong> If you entered Path at exactly level 56 (184,040 XP), the lamp brings you to at least <strong>189,040 XP</strong>, leaving at most <strong>710,217 XP</strong> to level 72 (899,257 XP). Cash sessions and earlier quests may have brought you much closer. While Guthix Sleeps awards another 80,000 Thieving XP, but you need 72 before starting it.</p>
        <p><strong>Check the quest journal and skill tab before speaking to Ivy Sophista in Taverley.</strong> Required quests: The Path of Glouphrie, Defender of Varrock, Fight Arena, Dream Mentor, The Hand in the Sand, Wanted!, Temple of the Eye (including Enter the Abyss), Tears of Guthix, Nature Spirit and A Tail of Two Cats; also <strong>180+ quest points</strong> and Warriors' Guild access. You need unboosted <strong>72 Thieving, 67 Magic, 66 Agility, 65 Farming, 65 Herblore and 62 Hunter</strong>, plus <strong>49+ Firemaking</strong> for the sapphire lantern. Your existing <strong>Attack + Strength ≥130</strong> gives Warriors' Guild access; a single 99 also qualifies. The earlier chapters and training above cover these requirements. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Update%3AWhile_Guthix_Sleeps#Requirements" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Jagex's WGS requirement announcement</a> and <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current detailed quest guide</a>.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Long quest, multiple banks:</strong> stage a small bank pile rather than carry everything at once. The route below groups the unusual items and spells by phase. Rebank before the Black Knight/Surok sequence and again before the Balance Elemental; Quest Helper can supply exact puzzle clicks, but it does not replace the supplies or spellbook checks here.</div>
        <ExpandableNote title="Gather the supplies for each phase of While Guthix Sleeps" label="Quest preparation">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Identity/infiltration:</strong> ring of charos(a) <em>or 500 coins</em>, knife, bronze med helm, iron chainbody, combat gear, food and travel teleports.</li>
            <li><strong>Investigation/serum:</strong> one ordinary log, <strong>one separate lantern lens</strong>, 20 coins for Betty's pink dye, and a seed dibber. Thaerisk supplies the snapdragon seed; keep it for the quest. Search the <strong>drawers south-east of Thaerisk</strong> for charcoal and papyrus. The hunting expert in Feldip Hills supplies the Mort myre fungus bait, so that part needs no fungus-farming trip.</li>
            <li><strong>Infiltration/temple:</strong> one unpowered orb and a <strong>lit sapphire lantern</strong>. In the Black Knights' Catacombs, the <strong>north-east table supplies Silif's lobster and ordinary restore potion</strong>. Keep both untouched for him; drinking the restore for your own stats creates a fresh shortage. Spade, hammer, chisel and the temple's herb-puzzle ingredients are obtained in the quest area.</li>
            <li><strong>Spell supplies:</strong> Lunar Astral Contact four times = <strong>8 air + 4 astral + 4 cosmic runes</strong>; a standard-spellbook Charge Orb = <strong>30 of its chosen elemental rune + 3 cosmic</strong>; additional runes for standard elemental attacks, binding, weakening, Telekinetic Grab and alchemy. Keep at least one each of air, water, earth, fire, mind, law and death for quest puzzles, with extra casts' worth where noted below.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Missing disguise pieces:</strong> buy the bronze med helm from <strong>Peksa in Barbarian Village</strong> and iron chainbody from <strong>Wayne in Falador</strong>. Buy a missing knife from the <strong>Lumbridge general store</strong>, and cut one ordinary tree for the log. The activated ring is a convenience; keep <strong>520 coins</strong> available if using the 500-coin alternative plus Betty's 20-coin dye.</p>
          <p><strong>Make the glass pieces:</strong> buy one bucket of sand and one soda ash per molten glass from a <strong>charter-ship Trader Crewmember</strong> such as Catherby's, and combine them at a furnace. Use a glassblowing pipe to make <strong>one lantern lens and one unpowered orb</strong>. If the pipe is missing, take the spawn in the <strong>glassblower's house on Entrana</strong>, banking weapons and armour before the Port Sarim boat. Reuse the pipe for later quests.</p>
          <p><strong>Recover a missing sapphire lantern:</strong> smith one steel bar into a bullseye lantern frame (49 Smithing), fit <strong>a glass-blown lantern lens</strong> (49 Crafting), and replace the lens with a <strong>cut sapphire</strong>. Have the Chemist in Rimmington turn one swamp tar from Lumbridge Swamp into lamp oil in his still, fill the lantern and light it (49 Firemaking). Keep any ordinary lens returned by the sapphire conversion for the serum phase; make a further loose lens only if that check is still short. If short of the bar, smelt one iron ore plus two coal; mine the sapphire from Shilo Village gem rocks and cut it if the bank has none. Stop when this one working lantern is ready, and retain it for later dark dungeons.</p>
          <p><strong>Runes and your own potions:</strong> buy the phase's missing runes from <strong>Baba Yaga on Lunar Isle</strong>, carrying the seal of passage, or use the appropriate unlocked rune shop. Count these after earlier spell use. Use <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer potions plus ordinary restore potions</a> for your own Prayer and stat recovery; banked super restores can combine those jobs. Silif's free potion is reserved for Silif.</p>
          <p>Keep these supplies in the bank and withdraw each phase's items as you need them. The <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quick guide</a> shows when to bring each item and where to collect supplies during the quest.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Investigation and alliance:</strong> begin with Ivy in Taverley, investigate Movario, then work with Thaerisk at the White Knights' Castle. Carry the ring/coin alternative, log and knife when the investigation calls for them; bring the lens, dye money, seed and dibber for the serum phase. Thaerisk can give a snapdragon seed. To recruit the four Slayer heroes efficiently, use the <strong>Lunar spell Astral Contact</strong> (67 Magic, astral runes) four times; Cyrisus must be contacted magically, while the others can be visited if you prefer. The spell was formerly called <em>NPC Contact</em>; older quest guides may still use that name. Bring the 8 air, 4 astral and 4 cosmic runes, then bank/regear after the alliance phase. Switch to the Lunar spellbook for Astral Contact; you unlocked it earlier. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps#Amassing_the_masters" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Alliance phase</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Astral_Contact" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current spell name</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Dark Squall and Surok:</strong> switch to the <strong>standard spellbook</strong> before the rune puzzles and Surok fight. Take bronze med helm, iron chainbody, unpowered orb, 30 runes of a chosen Charge Orb element plus 3 cosmic, and <strong>nine free inventory spaces</strong> for the infiltration. Do not rely on a powered staff for puzzle casts or for damaging Surok; he is immune to powered-staff damage. For Surok, pack runes for <strong>all four elemental attack spells</strong>, a bind (Snare/Entangle), a weakening spell (Weaken/Enfeeble), <strong>Telekinetic Grab</strong> and <strong>Low/High Alchemy</strong>: that means appropriate air/water/earth/fire plus mind/chaos/death as your chosen attacks require, body/soul for the chosen debuff, nature for alchemy and law for Telekinetic Grab. Recheck spellbook/rune pouch before entering. Bind his fast melee minion, weaken the strong one, telegrab then alch the explosive orb, and counter his elemental surges with the opposite element (fire with water, water with fire, air with earth, earth with air). Bring food and Prayers for the hostile knights and Surok; bank afterward. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current spell and puzzle sequence</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Chasm and temple:</strong> take the Dark Squall disguise when asked, a <strong>lit sapphire lantern</strong> for the Tears of Guthix chasm, Prayer points for Bloom, and room for the local puzzle supplies. Collect the druid pouch in the temple, cast Bloom near its roots, fill the pouch with the grown items and use it on the druid spirits for the required ingredients. Leave roughly seven free inventory slots; a spade, hammer and chisel can be obtained in the chasm. A games necklace reaches Tears of Guthix; climb down using the lantern/light creature route. Rebank after opening the temple's final door. Do not carry the whole investigation inventory into the boss room.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Balance Elemental—three styles, not two.</strong> Bring your existing dragon scimitar/defender melee setup, a Ranged weapon and ammunition from your bank (Ava's accumulator and your best appropriate bow or crossbow), and a Magic weapon/spell such as upgraded Iban's staff with its runes. Add <strong>Prayer potions plus ordinary restore potions</strong> (or banked super restores), <strong>strong food, a lit sapphire lantern and a non-rune emergency teleport</strong> such as an equipped teleport item; Magic can be drained to 1. A Menaphite remedy is helpful if already available, not a new mandatory potion grind. No Bowfa, blowpipe, black mask, Slayer helmet, Fire Cape, brews, Rigour or 90+ combats are assumed. The Elemental uses orange/fire <strong>Ranged</strong>, white/air <strong>Melee</strong> and blue/water <strong>Magic</strong>. Switch the matching protection prayer <em>as its appearance changes, before its next attack animation</em>; then switch your damage style to one it is not protecting against. It begins using protection prayers below half HP; late in the fight it protects against <strong>two styles at once</strong> and attacks faster, so a third damage style is required. Restore drained stats and Prayer, and use the <strong>Stone/pillars to break contact and slow the fight</strong> when overwhelmed: defensive prayer first, damage-style switch second. This is a mechanics check, not a DPS race. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps#Balancing_act" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current Balance Elemental mechanics</a>.</div>
        <p><strong>Quest Tormented Demons:</strong> after the Elemental, touch the <strong>Stone of Jas</strong>; it temporarily boosts your combat stats to <strong>255</strong> for the two quest demons. This is explicitly <em>not</em> a reason to pre-grind combat. Fight one at a time, keep the relevant protection prayer up, change your attack style around their protection prayers and move from targeted fire tiles. The Guardians of Armadyl assist. If supplies are low, teleport out and restock; the quest resumes at the demon phase without repeating the Elemental. A cautious player can hide behind the south-western column and let the Guardians do much of the work, but allow time and avoid idle logout. This is the <em>boosted quest encounter</em>, not normal post-quest Tormented Demon farming. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps#The_Stone_of_Jas" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Stone and demon phase</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Death risk:</strong> these are dangerous quest fights, not safe minigame deaths; Hardcore status is at stake. A Balance Elemental death places a grave <strong>by Movario and Darve in the Chasm of Tears</strong>, outside the boss area. You do not need another sapphire lantern merely to retrieve that grave, but you do need one to descend again afterward. Recover items before taking another risk. The south-west column is a quest-demon tactic, not a guaranteed safe spot for normal post-quest Tormented Demons. Teleporting out to bank is safer than pressing onward with exhausted supplies.</p>
        <p>Finish the dialogue and claim <strong>5 quest points; 80,000 Thieving, 75,000 Farming, 75,000 Herblore and 50,000 Hunter XP</strong>; and access to the <strong>Ancient Guthixian Temple and normal Tormented Demons</strong>. Afterward, speak to <strong>Kuradal in Shilo Village</strong> for <strong>Duradel's notes</strong>: their one-time Slayer XP is <strong>15 × your current Slayer level</strong> and they unlock the demonbane-weapon crafting path if a future synapse is obtained. Use the notes when convenient, then check your updated Slayer XP. Waiting many levels would add only a small amount of XP. A <strong>tormented synapse</strong> (for a future Scorching bow, Emberlight or Purging staff) is an optional upgrade to pursue when you feel ready. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Update%3AWhile_Guthix_Sleeps#Quest_Rewards" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Jagex rewards</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Kuradal" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Kuradal's notes</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Keep the next quest's balloon logs:</strong> after giving Movario's notes to Thaerisk, revisit the treasure room through the <strong>tunnel in the south-west corner of Movario's study</strong>. Its one-time loot includes <strong>100 unnoted magic logs</strong>. Keep at least <strong>three magic logs</strong> banked for Monkey Madness II's Grand Tree balloon unlock if that destination is still locked. Collecting the other 97 logs is optional. If you already looted the room, check that three logs remain in your bank and replace any missing logs before the balloon trip. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps#Rewards" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Movario's stored loot</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

